       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a potentially hepatotoxic dose, and I don't know of any clinical scenario that justifies it. Your patient has normal liver function and no unusual factors, so nothing in the chart explains it. If the order went through, the patient could be seriously harmed.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a safe dose.** I can enter 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours right now.\n- **Check the intent.** If this was a typo or a unit mix-up, tell me the dose you meant.\n- **Escalate.** If you think there's a real reason for a higher dose, please discuss it with your attending and a clinical pharmacist first. They can place or approve the order through the proper channels.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
